`docs/validation/repository-maintenance-20261109/report.md`.

| Criterion | Requirement / decision / risk / task | Method and observation | State and limits |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| AC-01 | REQ-01 / D-01 / R-01 / T001 | Source/local inventory; byte comparisons rejected duplicate-log deletion; empty placeholder removed | APPROVED; historical/unique data preserved |
| AC-02 | REQ-02 / D-02 / R-02 / T002 | Workflow owns closure, templates/shared skill integration link to it; three cases reviewed | APPROVED; documentary review does not prove autonomous agent compliance |
| AC-03 | REQ-03 / D-03 / R-03 / T003 | Real producer output and fixture lease checks; 16 migration hashes rechecked | APPROVED; legacy paths and Cargo environment preserved |
| AC-04 | REQ-04 / D-04 / R-04 / T004 | 23 filesystem/lifecycle fixtures; six independent succession tests | APPROVED within cooperative process boundary |
| AC-05 | REQ-05 / D-05 / R-05 / T005 | Broad regression plus affected-case rechecks, 23 final collector cases and three clean native static scans | APPROVED; one opt-in full scanner test not enabled, no product acceptance |

All adopted maintenance criteria are supported within the recorded boundary.
Task closure/documentation review and current content bindings are in evidence.json;
raw failures and successful rechecks remain in the report. Revisit pinned legacy
candidate data only with a retained-input/recovery-consumer review. Future input
changes invalidate only dependent observations. No new product acceptance is inferred.
